  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The letter of Anastasius to John of Jerusalem was written in the year 401; it is spoken of in Jerome’s Apol.",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "iii., c. 21, which was written in the first half of 402, as “the letter of last year.”",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Jerome intimates in the same passage that it was only one of several letters of the same character which Anastasius wrote to the East.",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Rufinus had not seen it, and refused to believe its genuineness. But there seems to be no reason for doubting this.",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Anastasius had, at the earnest request of Theophilus of Alexandria, formally condemned Origenism.",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s6",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And Rufinus’ translations of Origen’s Περὶ ᾽Αρχῶν and of Pamphilus’ Vindication of Origen,",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s7",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and his own book on the Falsification of Origen’s works were taken at Rome as a defence of Origenism generally.",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s8",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Rufinus, however, appealed continually, and especially in his Apology to Anastasius, to the church of Jerusalem, where he had been ordained.",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s9",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "“My faith,” he says, “is that which is preached at Jerusalem.” Anastasius, therefore, in condemning Origen would be understood as condemning Rufinus, and might also seem to condemn his Bishop John of Jerusalem.",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s10",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "This will account for the fulsome praises with which the letter opens. John, moreover, had written “to consult” Anastasius about Rufinus, which probably implies some action in Rufinus’ interest;",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.3.s11",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.3.s11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "but the fact that Jerome knew the contents of the letter and Rufinus did not seems to show that Bishop John had become more friendly with Jerome and less so with Rufinus.",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "1. The kind words of approval that you have addressed, my dear Bishop, to your brother Bishop, is a fresh mark of your long tried affection.",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "It is a high commendation which you confer upon me, a most lavish recognition of my services. I thank you for this proof of your love;",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and, following you at a distance in my littleness, I bring the tribute of my words to honour the splendour of your holiness and those virtues which the Lord has conferred upon you.",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "You excel all others so far, the splendour of your praise shines forth so conspicuously, that no words which I can use can equal your deserts.",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s5",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Yet your glory excites in me such admiration that I cannot turn away from the attempt to describe it, even though I can never do so adequately.",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s6",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And, first, the praise which you have bestowed on me out of the serene heaven of your great spirit forms part of your own glory:",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s7",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for it is the majesty of your episcopate, shining forth like the sun upon the opposite quarter of the world, which has reflected its own brightness upon us. And you give me your friendship unreservedly;",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s8",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "you do not weigh me in the balance of criticism. If it is right for you to praise me, must not your praise be echoed back to you?",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s9",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I beg you therefore, for your own sake no less than mine, that you will not praise me any more to my face.",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.4.s10",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.4.s10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I ask this for two reasons: if the praise is undeserved it must excite in your brother-bishop a sense of pain; if it is true, it must make him blush.",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.5.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.5.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "2. Let me come to the subject of your letter. Rufinus, about whom you have done me the honour to ask my advice, must bring his conscience to the bar of the divine majesty.",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.5.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.5.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "It is for him to see how he can approve himself to God as maintaining his true allegiance to him.",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.6.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.6.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "3. As for Origen, whose writings he has translated into our language, I have neither formerly known, nor do I now seek to know either who he was or what expression he may have given to his thought.",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.6.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.6.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But as to the feeling left by this matter on my own mind I should be glad to speak with your holiness for a moment.",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.6.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.6.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The impression which I have received is this,—and it has been brought out clearly by the reading of parts of Origen’s works by the people of our City,",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.6.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.6.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and by the sort of mist of blindness which it threw over them,—that his object was to disintegrate our faith, which is that of the Apostles, and has been confirmed by the traditions of the fathers, by leading us into tortuous paths.",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.7.s1",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.7.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "4. I want to know what is the meaning of the translation of this work into the Roman tongue.",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.7.s2",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.7.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If the translator intends by it to put the author in the wrong, and to denounce to the world his execrable deeds, well and good.",
    "chunk_index": 30,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.7.s3",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.7.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "In that case he will expose to well-merited hatred one who has long laboured under the adverse weight of public opinion.",
    "chunk_index": 31,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem#Anast.EpJoh.7.s4",
    "work_id": "npnf-works/anastasius-letter-to-john-of-jerusalem",
    "canonical_ref": "Anast.EpJoh.7.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But if by translating all these evil things he means to give his assent to them, and in that sense gives them to the world to read,",
    "chunk_index": 32,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 401,
    "date_range": [
      400,
      401
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
